+### 3.18 Volt
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Adapter ID | `volt` (`bench/adapters/volt.ts`) |
+| Maker, URL, license | Leul Aria, https://github.com/LeulAria/volt, MIT (a VS Code fork) |
+| Version | 0.0.6, 2026-11 (verify at freeze). Bundle `Volt.app`, bundle id `com.leularia.volt`, Electron |
+| On bench Mac | no |
+| Family | EL-SDK (Electron; agents over the Agent Client Protocol) |
+| Data to move aside | `~/Library/Application Support/Volt` (Electron profile, chats, the agent server's storage in `agentServer/`), `~/.volt` (sandbox state, worktrees, settings of Volt's own) |
+| Processes | Electron set; the agent server (the same `Electron` executable run as Node with `ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE=1`, entry `out/volt-agent-server-main.js`); `volt-sandbox-helper`; one `claude-agent-acp` (npx cache) per live chat with its `claude` child |
+| Claude runs via | `@agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp` 0.106.0 (Claude Agent SDK 0.3.322), which runs the system `claude` found on the login shell's PATH. Fetched with `npx` on first use into `~/.npm/_npx` |
+| Codex runs via | `codex-acp` over the system `codex` |
+| Adds to context | a lead block before the user's words (`[Volt]` notes and a short `<volt_workspace>` summary), the Volt MCP server's tools (host tools: browser, questions, threads, memory, render), and Claude Code's own system prompt. B2 shows the sizes |
+| Writes global config | none known (it reads `~/.claude`; Claude's config for a sandboxed chat lives under `~/.volt/sandbox/agent-state`) |
+| Pin | model Opus 5.5, effort High (factory: Medium) in the model picker; permissions Full access (factory: Supervised); sandbox factory default (workspace write) |
+| Side calls (B1) | thread title from the agent's `session_info_update`; Claude Code's own `count_tokens` calls at session start |
+| New thread (A3) | Cmd+N (a new draft in the current project, composer focused) |
+| Orchestration (C1) | subagents through Volt's `delegate_task` tool (Multitask), each in its own worktree |
+| Drive (setup) | `bin/code <folder>` CLI, the agent server's HTTP API, CDP |
+| Traps | the agent server is a launch agent that outlives a quit (A9 counts it); it lists Claude's models only when `~/.claude.json` names an account (an API-key-only login shows no Claude models); the first chat of a fresh profile installs the ACP adapter with npx |
+| Verify in pilot | composer and thread rects at 1600 x 1000 on a real screen; the C1 trigger |
+| Local only | "This Mac" in the composer's machine picker (factory). Check: the chat's machine chip reads This Mac |
+
+Adapter `volt`:
+
+| Method | How |
+|---|---|
+| `installCheck` | version and bundle SHA-256 of `/Applications/Volt.app` |
+| `reset` | default; data `~/Library/Application Support/Volt`, `~/.volt`; boot out `com.volt.agent-server.<hash>` |
+| `configure` | model Opus 5.5 High in the picker (the seed holds it), Full access (the seed holds it) |
+| `launch` | `open -a Volt` |
+| `newThread` | Cmd+N |
+| `send` | default |
+| `waitDone` | the Claude session log (cwd is the arena, or the chat's worktree) |
+| `quit` | default (Cmd+Q); the agent server keeps running by design |
+| `processes` | Electron set, the agent server and its children |
+
 ## 4. Summary
 
 | ADE | Adapter ID | Family | Drive for setup | C1 trigger | Top fairness traps |
@@ -837,4 +875,5 @@ Adapter `codex-app`:
 | Conductor | `conductor` | NATIVE | deep links, Accessibility | not supported | bundled CLI versions; new worktree plus setup script in A3 |
 | Capy | `capy` | OWN | HTTP API, CDP | subagents, Captains (experimental) | own harness; no Claude subscription, API billing |
 | Claude desktop | `claude-desktop` | FIRST | Accessibility | subagents, session messages | shares `~/.claude` with the CLI; stack unknown |
+| Volt | `volt` | EL-SDK | `bin/code` CLI, HTTP API, CDP | subagents through `delegate_task` | agent server outlives quit; Claude models need an account name |
 | Codex app | `codex-app` | FIRST | Accessibility | multi-agent (to verify) | moved into ChatGPT desktop; most facts unknown |
